          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000000",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Ras Sudr's Hidden Treasures: A Guide to Unparalleled Natural Wonders"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h2"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000005",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000003",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000002"
              ],
              "text": "Ras Sudr"
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000004",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": ", a serene getaway on the Red Sea coast, is a mosaic of stunning natural attractions. Each site offers a unique blend of beauty, adventure, and healing. Here are some must-visit spots that encapsulate the essence of this enchanting region."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000002",
              "_type": "internalLink",
              "reference": {
                "_ref": "wp-page-58907",
                "_type": "reference"
              }
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000007",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000006",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Hamamat Pharaon: A Sculpture Carved by Nature"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000000c",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000008",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Just 115 km from the Ahmad Hamdi Tunnel, Hamamat Pharaon is a marvel that words can barely do justice. The landscape here is nothing short of ethereal, with delicately carved rocks that form a natural sculpture of immense beauty. While it’s a place of relaxation and meditation, "
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000009"
              ],
              "text": "Hamamat Pharaon"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000000b",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " also beckons the adventurous. The area is ripe for exploration, from mountain climbing to off-the-beaten-path camping. Immerse yourself in the captivating colors of the mountains and valleys, each telling a story of time and nature."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000009",
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "https://www.egypttoday.com/Tag/30844/Hammam-Pharaon",
              "newTab": true
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000000e",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000d",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Eyoon Mousa: Where Nature Meets Spirituality"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000010",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "00000000000f",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "A short 14 km from Ahmad Hamdi Tunnel lies Eyoon Mousa, a natural spring rich in iodine and sulphur. Renowned for its therapeutic properties, particularly for skin ailments and rheumatism, Eyoon Mousa is more than a health retreat. It’s a place of spiritual and mental rejuvenation, offering a tranquil escape from the clamor of modern life. This site also holds special religious significance as the believed escape route of Moses from Pharaoh’s clutches. It’s an ideal spot for contemplation or simply enjoying the serene environment with loved ones."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000012",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000011",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Ein Malha: A Miracle in the Desert"
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000014",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000013",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Located 80 km from Ahmad Hamdi Tunnel, Ein Malha springs are not just a scenic spot for nature lovers but also a source of healing. The sulphate-rich hot waters, with temperatures ranging from 42°C to 73°C, have been known for their therapeutic effects on bone, joint, and rheumatic conditions. Locals celebrate these healing waters with festivals, embracing the springs’ gifts of health and longevity. Surrounded by palm trees and unspoiled nature, Ein Malha offers a peaceful retreat to reconnect with the world’s natural wonders."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
          "_key": "000000000016",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000015",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "Ein Yirga: A Winter Haven of Warmth "
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [],
          "style": "h3"
        },
        {
          "_key": "00000000001b",
          "_type": "block",
          "children": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000017",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": "50 km from Ahmad Hamdi Tunnel, Ein Yirga challenges the notion of "
            },
            {
              "_key": "000000000019",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [
                "000000000018"
              ],
              "text": "Ras Sudr"
            },
            {
              "_key": "00000000001a",
              "_type": "span",
              "marks": [],
              "text": " as solely a summer destination. The hot mineral-rich springs are a haven in cooler weather, offering detoxifying properties that benefit the digestive system and skin. For adrenaline seekers, Ein Yirga, nestled in a charming valley, presents the thrilling opportunity for a 30-meter dive into the warm springs. Developed as a tourist area by the Egyptian Government, it now draws both locals and tourists for relaxation and rejuvenation."
            }
          ],
          "markDefs": [
            {
              "_key": "000000000018",
              "_type": "externalLink",
              "href": "https://travel2egypt.org/ras-sudr-travel-guide/journey-sketches/",
              "newTab": false
            }
          ],
          "style": "normal"
        },
        {
